Very true, and very frustrating.

There's also the opposite problem of people who never learn, and keep
making the same mistakes in every company or project.  Weeding them out
(or at least most of them) seems to be a very rare skill.

It was interesting to see that the EV7 team avoided most of the biggest
problems that plagued the EV6 products.  Not by luck; they planned for
problems and built debugging tools that saved probably years of
time-to-market.  Of course new problems appeared, as they always do when
the design pushes the envelope.


