>
>I don't understand how they can own something that was sold before
>they bought DEC.  Am I confused about this "rights" business?

Compaq sold and/or bartered to Intel a non-exclusive license to use Alpha
IP, as well as ownership of the chip factory in Hudson, MA.   Probably a
few other miscellaneous tidbits as well.  I believe Compaq sold the
Fortran IP to Intel outright, with some additional contract terms around
future use and maintenance.

Compaq retained ownership of all the Alpha IP.  HP got that IP when they
bought Compaq.

Compaq developed the Alpha EV7 to be built with another company's
propriatary process, and all EV7 family parts have been made by that
company under contract.


