DEC would put your order in the queue if you signed a letter of
intent.
They'd ship your gear after they received your PO: sometimes weeks,
other times months, later. 
Once the gear was installed, they'd invoice you: sometimes they'd take
their own sweet time about sending out an installer, other times the
installer would be pulled off on a higher priority/paying job. 
Thirty days after receipt of invoice the company paid up. 

