The point I'm making, which you seem to have missed, is that Mentec
put *not one man-hour* of work into the *vintage* software. The
original owner bought it from DEC, twenty-five years later they give
it to me... whoops we lost the license documents years ago. By the
strict letter of the law, that means I'm expected to pay Mentec big
time before I can boot the machine. When they've done *nothing* for
me, my ancient hardware, or the ancient software I'm running. That's
what I mean by 'free money'. Every time a collector rescues an ancient
RSTS system, it's pure windfall for Mentec. 

If I wanted to run a current version of the OS, which Mentec had put a
lot of work into, that would of course be very different - but that's
*not* what I'm talking about.

>>                                               Legal it may be (though
>> it certainly is NOT legal in every jurisdiction), moral it sure hell
>> isn't IMHO.
>
