Hi,

I picked up a DECpc 433SE laptop at a thrift store.  Turns out the COM
port is set at 2400 baud.  I don't know the proper method of getting
into the bios, but if you boot with a non-bootable floppy in the drive
it gives you the opportunity to press F2 (doesn't work otherwise).  It
says "press F2 for setup utility".  Once pressed you are prompted to
"enter user password".  I've guessed many things with no luck.

There is also a special key marked Load Password.  When pressed it
searches the floppy drive and displays "Load Password processing", then
when it doesn't find what it is looking for it displays "it isn't the
support diskette...".

So, this has led me to believe that the bios is accessed via a special
floppy disk.  The bios is shown at boot as being version 2.00.  I'm
hoping that if it is flashable that doing so would reset the password.

Does anyone have a copy of the "support diskette" and/or a bios flash
file/utility?  I know that if I could disconnect the bios battery it
would reset, but the laptop case looks like a tough nut to crack.

Regards,
Doug

